### Update a page's title/icon, or archive it (write)

Archiving moves the page to trash; restoring brings it back.

### Update or archive a block (write)

Replacing a paragraph block's content requires the block to be a paragraph.

### Delete a block (write)

Moves the block to trash. To archive/restore a whole page, update the page.

## Output

Tool results are JSON. List tools return the items and whether more existed
past the limit; failures return the HTTP status and message — surface the
error rather than retrying blindly.

## Notes

- IDs are Notion object ids (UUIDs), with or without dashes. Get them from
  search, block, database, or query output.
- The integration's capabilities (read / write / comment) are set by the
  administrator on the Notion integration. A 401 / 403 usually means the
  integration lacks the needed capability or hasn't been shared with the
  page — tell the user rather than retrying.
